<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Theoretical Analysis</h2>

<div id="A1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">A complete theoretical analysis of the multi-agentic system ARM powered by LLMs is intractable due to the complex, high-dimensional nature of language generation and the non-stationary of the generation process. Therefore, to build a formal intuition for the design choices in our scaffolded search for the step-generator, and the decoupled search for the meta-policy (Algorithm<a href="#alg1" title="Algorithm 1 ‣ 4 ARM Search Algorithm ‣ ARM: Discovering Agentic Reasoning Modules for Generalizable Multi-Agent Systems" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>), we analyze an idealized formulation of the problem as a Markov Decision Process (MDP). This abstracts away the underlying complexities of the text generation and focuses on the dynamics of per-step error and state distribution shift. This analysis provides a formal argument for the soundness of our proposed search objective.</p>
</div>
<section id="A1.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.1 </span>An Idealized MDP Model of Step-wise Reasoning</h3>

<div id="A1.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We model the reasoning process as a Markov decision process (MDP) <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib36" title="" class="ltx_ref">Sutton &amp; Barto (2018)</a></cite> <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M}=(S,A,P,R,\gamma)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>S</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>P</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>R</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M}=(S,A,P,R,\gamma)</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<ul id="A1.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A1.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">State Space <math id="A1.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(S)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(S)</annotation></semantics></math>:</span> The state space <math id="A1.I1.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S=S_{ok}\cup S_{fail}\cup S_{done}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∪</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∪</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S=S_{ok}\cup S_{fail}\cup S_{done}</annotation></semantics></math> is partitioned into three disjoint subsets:</p>
<ul id="A1.I1.i1.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A1.I1.i1.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="A1.I1.i1.I1.i1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">–</span></span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i1.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.I1.i1.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A1.I1.i1.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{ok}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>S</mi><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{ok}</annotation></semantics></math>: A state <math id="A1.I1.i1.I1.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s\in S_{ok}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s\in S_{ok}</annotation></semantics></math> represents a partial reasoning trace <math id="A1.I1.i1.I1.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{q,p_{1},...p_{k}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{q,p_{1},...p_{k}}</annotation></semantics></math> that is on a valid path to a solution.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I1.i1.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="A1.I1.i1.I1.i2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">–</span></span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i1.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.I1.i1.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A1.I1.i1.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{fail}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>S</mi><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{fail}</annotation></semantics></math>: A state <math id="A1.I1.i1.I1.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s\in S_{fail}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s\in S_{fail}</annotation></semantics></math> has made a critical reasoning error from which recovery is not possible (including terminal states where the reasoning chain ended up on the wrong answer). This is an absorbing region.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I1.i1.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="A1.I1.i1.I1.i3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">–</span></span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i1.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.i1.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A1.I1.i1.I1.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{done}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>S</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{done}</annotation></semantics></math>: A state <math id="A1.I1.i1.I1.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s\in S_{done}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s\in S_{done}</annotation></semantics></math> represents a reasoning path that has successfully ended on the right answer. This is an absorbing region.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Action Space <math id="A1.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(A)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(A)</annotation></semantics></math></span>: For a fixed meta-policy <math id="A1.I1.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{Rec}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{Rec}</annotation></semantics></math> that recursively generates steps until termination (such as the one used by baseline CoT or the ARM-only variant), the meta policy executes a single action at any give state <math id="A1.I1.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s\in S_{ok}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s\in S_{ok}</annotation></semantics></math>: i.e., invokes a step-generator module <math id="A1.I1.i2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math> to produce the next reasoning step. Thus, the action space is a singleton <math id="A1.I1.i2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{A}=\{\texttt{generate\_step}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">generate_step</mtext><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{A}=\{\texttt{generate\_step}\}</annotation></semantics></math>. Hence, the choice of the module <math id="A1.I1.i2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math> fully defines the transition dynamics of the MDP.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I1.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Reward Function <math id="A1.I1.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(R)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(R)</annotation></semantics></math>: </span> A sparse reward function with <math id="A1.I1.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R=1</annotation></semantics></math> given upon transition to a done state.</p>
<ul id="A1.I1.i3.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A1.I1.i3.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="A1.I1.i3.I1.i1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">–</span></span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i3.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.i3.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A1.I1.i3.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R(s)=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R(s)=1</annotation></semantics></math> if <math id="A1.I1.i3.I1.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s\in S_{done}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s\in S_{done}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.I1.i3.I1.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math> otherwise.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I1.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.I1.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I1.i4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Transition Dynamics (P)</span>: update function (see 3.2.1) <math id="A1.I1.i4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U_{m,.}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>U</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U_{m,.}</annotation></semantics></math> where <math id="A1.I1.i4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m\in\mathcal{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m\in\mathcal{M}</annotation></semantics></math> is characterized by its state-dependent error rate, <math id="A1.I1.i4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon_{m}(s)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon_{m}(s)</annotation></semantics></math>, which is the probability of making a catastrophic irrecoverable error from state <math id="A1.I1.i4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>s</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s</annotation></semantics></math>. Additionally, we introduce For any state <math id="A1.I1.i4.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s\in S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s\in S</annotation></semantics></math>, the transition probabilities to the next state <math id="A1.I1.i4.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> are defined as:</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.I1.i4.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<ul id="A1.I1.i4.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A1.I1.i4.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="A1.I1.i4.I1.i1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">–</span></span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i4.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.I1.i4.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A1.I1.i4.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P(s^{\prime}|s,m)=\begin{cases}p_{done}(s)&amp;\text{if }s^{\prime}\in S_{done}\\
\epsilon_{m}(s)&amp;\text{if }s^{\prime}\in S_{fail}\\
1-p_{done}(s)-\epsilon_{m}(s)&amp;\text{if }s^{\prime}\in S_{ok}\end{cases}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mtext>if </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mtext>if </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mtext>if </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P(s^{\prime}|s,m)=\begin{cases}p_{done}(s)&amp;\text{if }s^{\prime}\in S_{done}\\
\epsilon_{m}(s)&amp;\text{if }s^{\prime}\in S_{fail}\\
1-p_{done}(s)-\epsilon_{m}(s)&amp;\text{if }s^{\prime}\in S_{ok}\end{cases}</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.I1.i4.I1.i1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.i4.I1.i1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Note that <math id="A1.I1.i4.I1.i1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{done}(s)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{done}(s)</annotation></semantics></math> is the intrinsic probability of finishing the task by transitioning into a done state from state <math id="A1.I1.i4.I1.i1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>s</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s</annotation></semantics></math>. In practice, this is when the model emits <span id="A1.I1.i4.I1.i1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">//boxed[Correct Answer]</span>. This can be assumed to be a property of the task and the progress so far, rather than the generator itself.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I1.i5" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.i5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I1.i5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Value Function:</span> The value of a state <math id="A1.I1.i5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>s</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s</annotation></semantics></math> under module <math id="A1.I1.i5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math>, denoted by <math id="A1.I1.i5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{m}(s)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{m}(s)</annotation></semantics></math> is the probability of eventually reaching a success state in <math id="A1.I1.i5.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{done}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>S</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{done}</annotation></semantics></math> (thus receiving a reward) starting from <math id="A1.I1.i5.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>s</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Within in MDP framework, the ideal objective is to discover a module <math id="A1.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>m</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m^{*}</annotation></semantics></math>, that maximizes the expected value from the initial state distribution <math id="A1.SS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{0}(s)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{0}(s)</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<table id="A1.Ex4" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m^{*}=\underset{m\in\mathcal{M}}{\text{arg\, max}\,}\mathbb{E}_{s_{0}\sim d_{0}(s)}\left[V_{m}(s_{0})\right]" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>m</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><munder accentunder="true"><mtext>arg  max</mtext><mrow><mi mathsize="0.700em">m</mi><mo mathsize="0.700em">∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathsize="0.700em">ℳ</mi></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>∼</mo><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m^{*}=\underset{m\in\mathcal{M}}{\text{arg\, max}\,}\mathbb{E}_{s_{0}\sim d_{0}(s)}\left[V_{m}(s_{0})\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">This objective poses several major optimization challenges: 1) credit assignment problem over long sequence of steps and 2) unconstrained search space of code modules.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.2 </span>Theoretical Grounding for the Scaffolded Step-Generator Search</h3>

<div id="A1.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The scaffolded objective evaluates a candidate <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math> by <em id="A1.SS2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">splicing</em> it into a baseline rollout for a short window
<math id="A1.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\in\{i,\dots,i+\ell-1\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\in\{i,\dots,i+\ell-1\}</annotation></semantics></math> while keeping <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m_{\text{CoT}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>m</mi><mtext>CoT</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m_{\text{CoT}}</annotation></semantics></math> before and after:</p>
<table id="A1.Ex5" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\underbrace{U^{*}_{m_{\text{CoT}}}\circ\big(\,U^{\ell}_{m}\,\big)\circ U^{i}_{m_{\text{CoT}}}}_{\text{\textquotedblleft baseline\textendash candidate\textendash baseline\textquotedblright}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><msubsup><mi>U</mi><msub><mi>m</mi><mtext>CoT</mtext></msub><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.170em">(</mo><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mi>m</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msubsup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.055em">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msubsup><mi>U</mi><msub><mi>m</mi><mtext>CoT</mtext></msub><mi>i</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mtext>“baseline–candidate–baseline”</mtext></munder><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\underbrace{U^{*}_{m_{\text{CoT}}}\circ\big(\,U^{\ell}_{m}\,\big)\circ U^{i}_{m_{\text{CoT}}}}_{\text{\textquotedblleft baseline\textendash candidate\textendash baseline\textquotedblright}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{\text{CoT},t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mtext>CoT</mtext><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{\text{CoT},t}</annotation></semantics></math> be the state distribution at step <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> along the (unperturbed) baseline trace.
Define the single-step advantage <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{m}(s)\coloneqq V_{m}(s)-V_{\text{CoT}}(s)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mtext>CoT</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{m}(s)\coloneqq V_{m}(s)-V_{\text{CoT}}(s)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmassumption1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_assumption">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmassumption1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Assumption 1</span></span><span id="Thmassumption1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Finite-horizon conditional stability)<span id="Thmassumption1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmassumption1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Thmassumption1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmassumption1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Within the scaffold window and for states along the baseline trace (<math id="Thmassumption1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s\sim d_{\text{CoT},t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">CoT</mtext><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s\sim d_{\text{CoT},t}</annotation></semantics></math>),
the <em id="Thmassumption1.p1.1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_upright">conditional</em> next-state distributions inside <math id="Thmassumption1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{S}_{ok}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{S}_{ok}</annotation></semantics></math> remain close:</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex6" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex6.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{s\sim d_{\text{CoT},t}}\Big[D_{\mathrm{TV}}\big(T_{m}(\cdot\mid s,\mathcal{S}_{ok})\,\|\,T_{\text{CoT}}(\cdot\mid s,\mathcal{S}_{ok})\big)\Big]\;\leq\;\beta_{ok}\quad\forall t\in\{i,\dots,i+\ell-1\}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">CoT</mtext><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">[</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>TV</mi></msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0.337em">∥</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">CoT</mtext></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" rspace="0.280em">]</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">≤</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{s\sim d_{\text{CoT},t}}\Big[D_{\mathrm{TV}}\big(T_{m}(\cdot\mid s,\mathcal{S}_{ok})\,\|\,T_{\text{CoT}}(\cdot\mid s,\mathcal{S}_{ok})\big)\Big]\;\leq\;\beta_{ok}\quad\forall t\in\{i,\dots,i+\ell-1\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<ul id="A1.I2" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A1.I2.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I2.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.I2.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I2.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Remark:</span> This constraint requires that, conditional on the trajectory staying in <math id="A1.I2.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{ok}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>S</mi><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{ok}</annotation></semantics></math>, the distribution over possible next states under module <math id="A1.I2.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math> is close on average (in total variation distance) to the distribution under <math id="A1.I2.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m_{\text{CoT}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>m</mi><mtext>CoT</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m_{\text{CoT}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.I2.i1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.I2.i1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">This assumption is grounded in the mechanics of the prompted LLMs. The scaffold provides a strong contextual prior (the preceding CoT steps) and acts as a powerful inductive bias, strongly constraining the module to generate a next step that is stylistically and logically consistent with the atomic reasoning style of CoT. For instance, by defining variables in the same format, using consistent LaTeX for equations, or following an established deductive pattern (e.g., ’<span id="A1.I2.i1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">Let x be..., then it follows that y..., therefore z...</span>’ etc.). This incentivizes the LLM to generate a coherent and logically plausible continuation—a necessary condition for remaining in <math id="A1.I2.i1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{ok}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>S</mi><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{ok}</annotation></semantics></math>. Therefore, any “successful” module <math id="A1.I2.i1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math> must, by necessity, learn to mimic the local <em id="A1.I2.i1.p2.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">successful</em> behavior of <math id="A1.I2.i1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m_{CoT}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>m</mi><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m_{CoT}</annotation></semantics></math> while minimizing the transition probability to hazard states <math id="A1.I2.i1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{fail}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>S</mi><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{fail}</annotation></semantics></math>. This is empirically supported by the examples shown in Appendix-<a href="#A2" title="Appendix B Step Generator roll out Examples ‣ ARM: Discovering Agentic Reasoning Modules for Generalizable Multi-Agent Systems" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B</span></a>.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
<div id="Thmproposition1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_proposition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmproposition1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proposition 1</span></span><span id="Thmproposition1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Scaffolded objective optimizes per-step error rate)<span id="Thmproposition1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmproposition1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Thmproposition1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmproposition1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="Thmproposition1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> be the probability the baseline remains in <math id="Thmproposition1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{S}_{ok}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{S}_{ok}</annotation></semantics></math> up to step <math id="Thmproposition1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>.
Then for a universal constant <math id="Thmproposition1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex7" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{\text{scaffold}}(m)-V_{\text{scaffold}}(m_{\text{CoT}})\;\geq\;\sum_{t=i}^{i+\ell-1}\mathbb{E}_{s\sim d_{\text{CoT},t}}\!\big[A_{m}(s)\big]\;-\;C\sum_{t=i}^{i+\ell-1}w_{t}\,\beta_{ok}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">scaffold</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">scaffold</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">CoT</mtext></msub><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.391em">≥</mo><mrow><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">CoT</mtext><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.280em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.502em">−</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{\text{scaffold}}(m)-V_{\text{scaffold}}(m_{\text{CoT}})\;\geq\;\sum_{t=i}^{i+\ell-1}\mathbb{E}_{s\sim d_{\text{CoT},t}}\!\big[A_{m}(s)\big]\;-\;C\sum_{t=i}^{i+\ell-1}w_{t}\,\beta_{ok}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmproposition1.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmproposition1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Moreover, under Assumption <a href="#Thmassumption1" title="Assumption 1 (Finite-horizon conditional stability). ‣ A.2 Theoretical Grounding for the Scaffolded Step-Generator Search ‣ Appendix A Theoretical Analysis ‣ ARM: Discovering Agentic Reasoning Modules for Generalizable Multi-Agent Systems" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>, <math id="Thmproposition1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{m}(s)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{m}(s)</annotation></semantics></math> is dominated by <em id="Thmproposition1.p1.2.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_upright">error-rate reduction</em>:</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex8" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex8.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="A_{m}(s)\;\approx\;\big(\varepsilon_{\text{CoT}}(s)-\varepsilon_{m}(s)\big)\cdot\mathbb{E}_{s^{\prime}\sim T_{\text{CoT}}(\cdot\mid s,\mathcal{S}_{ok})}\!\big[V_{\text{CoT}}(s^{\prime})\big]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">≈</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msub><mi>ε</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">CoT</mtext></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.055em">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∼</mo><mi>T</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">CoT</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">CoT</mtext></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{m}(s)\;\approx\;\big(\varepsilon_{\text{CoT}}(s)-\varepsilon_{m}(s)\big)\cdot\mathbb{E}_{s^{\prime}\sim T_{\text{CoT}}(\cdot\mid s,\mathcal{S}_{ok})}\!\big[V_{\text{CoT}}(s^{\prime})\big].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof of Proposition <a href="#Thmproposition1" title="Proposition 1 (Scaffolded objective optimizes per-step error rate). ‣ A.2 Theoretical Grounding for the Scaffolded Step-Generator Search ‣ Appendix A Theoretical Analysis ‣ ARM: Discovering Agentic Reasoning Modules for Generalizable Multi-Agent Systems" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>.</h6>
<div id="A1.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">By Assumption-<a href="#Thmassumption1" title="Assumption 1 (Finite-horizon conditional stability). ‣ A.2 Theoretical Grounding for the Scaffolded Step-Generator Search ‣ Appendix A Theoretical Analysis ‣ ARM: Discovering Agentic Reasoning Modules for Generalizable Multi-Agent Systems" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>, the performance improvement within the <math id="A1.SS2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="l" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>l</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">l</annotation></semantics></math>-step scaffold window is lower bounded by the cumulative advantage, minus a small penalty for the distribution shift on successful steps <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib16" title="" class="ltx_ref">Kakade &amp; Langford (2002)</a>; <a href="#bib.bib33" title="" class="ltx_ref">Schulman et al. (2015)</a></cite>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_underline ltx_font_italic">Side Note:</span><span id="A1.SS2.p4.1.2" class="ltx_text"> For the purpose of a conservative lower bound, we treat this term
as a penalty. However, in practice such conditional distributional shift may be
beneficial: an advanced module <math id="A1.SS2.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math>, potentially using mechanisms like self-consistency
or debate, could guide the trajectory toward higher-value states even within
<math id="A1.SS2.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{S}_{ok}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{S}_{ok}</annotation></semantics></math>. This would add a positive contribution, but our main result does
not rely on that stronger assumption.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">For a step <math id="A1.SS2.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> and a baseline state <math id="A1.SS2.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s\in\mathcal{S}_{ok}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s\in\mathcal{S}_{ok}</annotation></semantics></math>, the Bellman equation with our transitions gives</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex9" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex9.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="V_{m}(s)=p_{\text{done}}(s)\cdot 1+\big(1-p_{\text{done}}(s)-\varepsilon_{m}(s)\big)\cdot\mathbb{E}_{s^{\prime}\sim T_{m}(\cdot\mid s,\mathcal{S}_{ok})}\big[V_{m}(s^{\prime})\big]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mtext>done</mtext></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mtext>done</mtext></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.055em">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∼</mo><mi>T</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{m}(s)=p_{\text{done}}(s)\cdot 1+\big(1-p_{\text{done}}(s)-\varepsilon_{m}(s)\big)\cdot\mathbb{E}_{s^{\prime}\sim T_{m}(\cdot\mid s,\mathcal{S}_{ok})}\big[V_{m}(s^{\prime})\big].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.p5.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p5.2.1" class="ltx_text">Subtract the corresponding identity for <math id="A1.SS2.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{\text{CoT}}(s)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mtext>CoT</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{\text{CoT}}(s)</annotation></semantics></math> and rearrange:</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx1" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex10"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle A_{m}(s)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle A_{m}(s)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex10.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=V_{m}(s)-V_{\text{CoT}}(s)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mtext>CoT</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=V_{m}(s)-V_{\text{CoT}}(s)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex11"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\underbrace{\big(\varepsilon_{\text{CoT}}(s)-\varepsilon_{m}(s)\big)\,\mathbb{E}_{s^{\prime}\sim T_{\text{CoT}}(\cdot\mid s,\mathcal{S}_{ok})}\!\big[V_{\text{CoT}}(s^{\prime})\big]}_{\text{error-rate reduction term}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mi>ε</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mtext>CoT</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>−</mo><mi>ε</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.170em">)</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>s</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∼</mo><mi>T</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mtext>CoT</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mi>V</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mtext>CoT</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mtext>error-rate reduction term</mtext></munder></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\underbrace{\big(\varepsilon_{\text{CoT}}(s)-\varepsilon_{m}(s)\big)\,\mathbb{E}_{s^{\prime}\sim T_{\text{CoT}}(\cdot\mid s,\mathcal{S}_{ok})}\!\big[V_{\text{CoT}}(s^{\prime})\big]}_{\text{error-rate reduction term}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex12"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\quad+\underbrace{\big(1-p_{\text{done}}(s)-\varepsilon_{m}(s)\big)\,\big(\mathbb{E}_{s^{\prime}\sim T_{m}}[V_{m}(s^{\prime})]-\mathbb{E}_{s^{\prime}\sim T_{\text{CoT}}}[V_{\text{CoT}}(s^{\prime})]\big)}_{\triangle(s)}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>+</mo><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mtext>done</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mtext>CoT</mtext></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mtext>CoT</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">△</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></munder></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\quad+\underbrace{\big(1-p_{\text{done}}(s)-\varepsilon_{m}(s)\big)\,\big(\mathbb{E}_{s^{\prime}\sim T_{m}}[V_{m}(s^{\prime})]-\mathbb{E}_{s^{\prime}\sim T_{\text{CoT}}}[V_{\text{CoT}}(s^{\prime})]\big)}_{\triangle(s)}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.p5.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p5.3.1" class="ltx_text">By Assumption <a href="#Thmassumption1" title="Assumption 1 (Finite-horizon conditional stability). ‣ A.2 Theoretical Grounding for the Scaffolded Step-Generator Search ‣ Appendix A Theoretical Analysis ‣ ARM: Discovering Agentic Reasoning Modules for Generalizable Multi-Agent Systems" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>, the conditional distributions inside <math id="A1.SS2.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{S}_{ok}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{S}_{ok}</annotation></semantics></math> are close in total variation, hence (by standard TV–expectation inequalities) for some constant <math id="A1.SS2.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C^{\prime}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>C</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C^{\prime}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex13" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\big|\mathbb{E}_{s^{\prime}\sim T_{m}}[V_{m}(s^{\prime})]-\mathbb{E}_{s^{\prime}\sim T_{\text{CoT}}}[V_{\text{CoT}}(s^{\prime})]\big|\;\leq\;C^{\prime}\,\beta_{ok}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mtext>CoT</mtext></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mtext>CoT</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.280em" stretchy="true">|</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">≤</mo><mrow><msup><mi>C</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\big|\mathbb{E}_{s^{\prime}\sim T_{m}}[V_{m}(s^{\prime})]-\mathbb{E}_{s^{\prime}\sim T_{\text{CoT}}}[V_{\text{CoT}}(s^{\prime})]\big|\;\leq\;C^{\prime}\,\beta_{ok}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.p5.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p5.4.1" class="ltx_text">Since <math id="A1.SS2.p5.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0\leq 1-p_{\text{done}}(s)-\varepsilon_{m}(s)\leq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mtext>done</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0\leq 1-p_{\text{done}}(s)-\varepsilon_{m}(s)\leq 1</annotation></semantics></math>, we have <math id="A1.SS2.p5.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\triangle(s)|\leq C^{\prime}\beta_{ok}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">△</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msup><mi>C</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\triangle(s)|\leq C^{\prime}\beta_{ok}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Taking expectations over <math id="A1.SS2.p5.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s\sim d_{\text{CoT},t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mtext>CoT</mtext><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s\sim d_{\text{CoT},t}</annotation></semantics></math> and summing from <math id="A1.SS2.p5.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t=i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t=i</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="A1.SS2.p5.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i+\ell-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i+\ell-1</annotation></semantics></math>,
the additive “shift” terms accumulate only along trajectories that have not yet absorbed,
which contributes the factor <math id="A1.SS2.p5.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>; let <math id="A1.SS2.p5.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C\geq C^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>≥</mo><msup><mi>C</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C\geq C^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> absorb constants and the bound on <math id="A1.SS2.p5.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{t}\leq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{t}\leq 1</annotation></semantics></math>.
This yields the stated lower bound. The approximation claim follows by dropping <math id="A1.SS2.p5.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\triangle(s)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">△</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\triangle(s)</annotation></semantics></math>,
which is precisely the small conditional-shift term bounded via <math id="A1.SS2.p5.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{ok}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>β</mi><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{ok}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text">This leaves an approximation where the advantage is primarily driven by the reduction in the probability of making a catastrophic error. This proposition is directly supported by the empirical results in Figure-<a href="#S7.F3" title="Figure 3 ‣ 7.1 Empirical Validation of the Step-Generator Objective ‣ 7 Analyses ‣ ARM: Discovering Agentic Reasoning Modules for Generalizable Multi-Agent Systems" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>, which shows a strong correlation between a module’s rank and its per-step error rate.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.3 </span>Theoretical Grounding for the Decoupled Meta-Policy Search</h3>

<div id="A1.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We now justify the zero-shot transfer of a meta-policy <math id="A1.SS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi^{\ast}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi^{\ast}</annotation></semantics></math> discovered using the surrogate <math id="A1.SS3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m_{\text{CoT}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>m</mi><mtext>CoT</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m_{\text{CoT}}</annotation></semantics></math> to the final module <math id="A1.SS3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m^{\ast}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>m</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m^{\ast}</annotation></semantics></math>. The goal is to show that the expected value of the full system improves, i.e.,</p>
<table id="A1.Ex14" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V(\pi^{\ast}(m^{\ast}))\;\geq\;V(\pi^{\ast}(m_{\text{CoT}}))." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>m</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">≥</mo><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mtext>CoT</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V(\pi^{\ast}(m^{\ast}))\;\geq\;V(\pi^{\ast}(m_{\text{CoT}})).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="Thmproposition2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_proposition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmproposition2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proposition 2</span></span><span id="Thmproposition2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Module improvement on baseline states)<span id="Thmproposition2.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmproposition2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Thmproposition2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmproposition2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">The scaffolded meta policy objective optimizes for a module <math id="Thmproposition2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m^{\ast}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>m</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m^{\ast}</annotation></semantics></math> that has a non-negative expected advantage over the states induced by the baseline policy:</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex15" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{s\sim d_{m_{\text{CoT}}}}[V_{m^{\ast}}(s)]\;\geq\;\mathbb{E}_{s\sim d_{m_{\text{CoT}}}}[V(s)]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><msub><mi>m</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">CoT</mtext></msub></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><msup><mi>m</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">≥</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><msub><mi>m</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">CoT</mtext></msub></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{s\sim d_{m_{\text{CoT}}}}[V_{m^{\ast}}(s)]\;\geq\;\mathbb{E}_{s\sim d_{m_{\text{CoT}}}}[V(s)].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmproposition3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_proposition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmproposition3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proposition 3</span></span><span id="Thmproposition3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Beneficial distribution shift)<span id="Thmproposition3.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmproposition3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Thmproposition3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmproposition3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">A superior module <math id="Thmproposition3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m^{\ast}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>m</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m^{\ast}</annotation></semantics></math>, which has a lower error rate on-expectation compared to the baseline (i.e., <math id="Thmproposition3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{s\sim d_{m_{\text{CoT}}}}[\epsilon_{m^{\ast}}(s)]\leq\mathbb{E}_{s\sim d_{m_{\text{CoT}}}}[\epsilon_{m_{\text{CoT}}}(s)]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><msub><mi>m</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">CoT</mtext></msub></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><msup><mi>m</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><msub><mi>m</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">CoT</mtext></msub></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><msub><mi>m</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">CoT</mtext></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{s\sim d_{m_{\text{CoT}}}}[\epsilon_{m^{\ast}}(s)]\leq\mathbb{E}_{s\sim d_{m_{\text{CoT}}}}[\epsilon_{m_{\text{CoT}}}(s)]</annotation></semantics></math>), induces a stationary state distribution <math id="Thmproposition3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{m^{\ast}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>d</mi><msup><mi>m</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{m^{\ast}}</annotation></semantics></math> that is weighted towards higher-value states.</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex16" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{s\sim d_{m^{*}}}\big[V_{m^{*}}(s)\big]\;\geq\;\mathbb{E}_{s\sim d_{\text{CoT}}}\big[V_{m^{*}}(s)\big]" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><msup><mi>m</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><msup><mi>m</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.280em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">≥</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">CoT</mtext></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><msup><mi>m</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{s\sim d_{m^{*}}}\big[V_{m^{*}}(s)\big]\;\geq\;\mathbb{E}_{s\sim d_{\text{CoT}}}\big[V_{m^{*}}(s)\big]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<ul id="A1.I3" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A1.I3.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I3.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I3.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I3.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Remark:</span> Reducing per-step hazard (<math id="A1.I3.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{fail}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>S</mi><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{fail}</annotation></semantics></math> states) increases expected survival time in <math id="A1.I3.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{S}_{ok}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{S}_{ok}</annotation></semantics></math>, shifting probability away from <math id="A1.I3.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{S}_{fail}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{S}_{fail}</annotation></semantics></math>. Since <math id="A1.I3.i1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{m^{\ast}}(s)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><msup><mi>m</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{m^{\ast}}(s)</annotation></semantics></math> is larger on <math id="A1.I3.i1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{S}_{ok}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{S}_{ok}</annotation></semantics></math> than on <math id="A1.I3.i1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{S}_{fail}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{S}_{fail}</annotation></semantics></math>, the expected value under <math id="A1.I3.i1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{m^{\ast}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>d</mi><msup><mi>m</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{m^{\ast}}</annotation></semantics></math> is weakly greater.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS3.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS3.p3.1" class="ltx_p">We now justify the zero-shot transfer of a meta-policy <math id="A1.SS3.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> discovered using the surrogate <math id="A1.SS3.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m_{CoT}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>m</mi><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m_{CoT}</annotation></semantics></math> to the final module <math id="A1.SS3.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>m</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m^{*}</annotation></semantics></math>. We aim to show that the expected value of the system improves: <math id="A1.SS3.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\overline{V}_{m^{*}}\geq\overline{V}_{m_{CoT}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><msup><mi>m</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msub><mo>≥</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><msub><mi>m</mi><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\overline{V}_{m^{*}}\geq\overline{V}_{m_{CoT}}</annotation></semantics></math>. This transfer relies on two premises.

<br class="ltx_break"></p>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem 1</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Monotonic Improvement of Meta-Policy Transfer)<span id="Thmtheorem1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Thmtheorem1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="Thmtheorem1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi(m)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi(m)</annotation></semantics></math> denote the system using meta-policy <math id="Thmtheorem1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>π</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi</annotation></semantics></math> and step-generator <math id="Thmtheorem1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math>, and let <math id="Thmtheorem1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V(\pi(m))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V(\pi(m))</annotation></semantics></math> be its expected reward from the initial state distribution. If Proposition <a href="#Thmproposition2" title="Proposition 2 (Module improvement on baseline states). ‣ A.3 Theoretical Grounding for the Decoupled Meta-Policy Search ‣ Appendix A Theoretical Analysis ‣ ARM: Discovering Agentic Reasoning Modules for Generalizable Multi-Agent Systems" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> and Proposition <a href="#Thmproposition3" title="Proposition 3 (Beneficial distribution shift). ‣ A.3 Theoretical Grounding for the Decoupled Meta-Policy Search ‣ Appendix A Theoretical Analysis ‣ ARM: Discovering Agentic Reasoning Modules for Generalizable Multi-Agent Systems" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a> hold, then the transfer of a meta-policy <math id="Thmtheorem1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi^{\ast}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi^{\ast}</annotation></semantics></math> from <math id="Thmtheorem1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m_{\text{CoT}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>m</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">CoT</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m_{\text{CoT}}</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="Thmtheorem1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m^{\ast}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>m</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m^{\ast}</annotation></semantics></math> is guaranteed to not degrade performance:</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex17" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V(\pi^{\ast}(m^{\ast}))\;\geq\;V(\pi^{\ast}(m_{\text{CoT}}))." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>m</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">≥</mo><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">CoT</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V(\pi^{\ast}(m^{\ast}))\;\geq\;V(\pi^{\ast}(m_{\text{CoT}})).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<section id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Proof Sketch: </h5>

<div id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We can decompose the difference in expected values as follows:</p>
<table id="A1.Ex18" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V(\pi^{\ast}(m^{\ast}))-V(\pi^{\ast}(m_{\text{CoT}}))=\mathbb{E}_{s\sim d_{m^{\ast}}}[V_{m^{\ast}}(s)]-\mathbb{E}_{s\sim d_{m_{\text{CoT}}}}[V(s)]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>m</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mtext>CoT</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><msup><mi>m</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><msup><mi>m</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><msub><mi>m</mi><mtext>CoT</mtext></msub></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V(\pi^{\ast}(m^{\ast}))-V(\pi^{\ast}(m_{\text{CoT}}))=\mathbb{E}_{s\sim d_{m^{\ast}}}[V_{m^{\ast}}(s)]-\mathbb{E}_{s\sim d_{m_{\text{CoT}}}}[V(s)].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">We can add and subtract the term <math id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{s\sim d_{m_{\text{CoT}}}}[V_{m^{\ast}}(s)]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><msub><mi>m</mi><mtext>CoT</mtext></msub></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><msup><mi>m</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{s\sim d_{m_{\text{CoT}}}}[V_{m^{\ast}}(s)]</annotation></semantics></math> to obtain:</p>
<table id="A1.Ex19" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex19X"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex19X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle V(\pi^{\ast}(m^{\ast}))-V(\pi^{\ast}(m_{\text{CoT}}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>m</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mtext>CoT</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle V(\pi^{\ast}(m^{\ast}))-V(\pi^{\ast}(m_{\text{CoT}}))</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex19X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\underbrace{\Big(\mathbb{E}_{s\sim d_{m^{\ast}}}[V_{m^{\ast}}(s)]-\mathbb{E}_{s\sim d_{m_{\text{CoT}}}}[V_{m^{\ast}}(s)]\Big)}_{\text{Gain from Distribution Shift}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><msup><mi>m</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><msup><mi>m</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><msub><mi>m</mi><mtext>CoT</mtext></msub></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><msup><mi>m</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mtext>Gain from Distribution Shift</mtext></munder></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\underbrace{\Big(\mathbb{E}_{s\sim d_{m^{\ast}}}[V_{m^{\ast}}(s)]-\mathbb{E}_{s\sim d_{m_{\text{CoT}}}}[V_{m^{\ast}}(s)]\Big)}_{\text{Gain from Distribution Shift}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex19Xa"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex19Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle+\underbrace{\Big(\mathbb{E}_{s\sim d_{m_{\text{CoT}}}}[V_{m^{\ast}}(s)]-\mathbb{E}_{s\sim d_{m_{\text{CoT}}}}[V(s)]\Big)}_{\text{Gain from Module Improvement}}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>+</mo><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><msub><mi>m</mi><mtext>CoT</mtext></msub></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><msup><mi>m</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><msub><mi>m</mi><mtext>CoT</mtext></msub></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mtext>Gain from Module Improvement</mtext></munder></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle+\underbrace{\Big(\mathbb{E}_{s\sim d_{m_{\text{CoT}}}}[V_{m^{\ast}}(s)]-\mathbb{E}_{s\sim d_{m_{\text{CoT}}}}[V(s)]\Big)}_{\text{Gain from Module Improvement}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The first term (<em id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Gain from Distribution Shift</em>) is non-negative by Proposition-3. The second term (<em id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p2.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Gain from Module Improvement</em>) is non-negative by Proposition-2. Since both terms are non-negative, their sum is non-negative, proving the theorem.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">This theoretical decomposition is empirically validated by the experiment in Figure <a href="#S7.F3" title="Figure 3 ‣ 7.1 Empirical Validation of the Step-Generator Objective ‣ 7 Analyses ‣ ARM: Discovering Agentic Reasoning Modules for Generalizable Multi-Agent Systems" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>. The performance of <em id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">CoT<math id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\to" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\to</annotation></semantics></math>Meta</em> relative to <em id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p3.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">CoT Baseline</em> measures the Gain from Module Improvement, while the additional gain seen in the full <em id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p3.1.3" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Meta Policy</em> system reflects the Gain from Distribution Shift. The positive results for both components provide strong empirical support for this theoretical justification.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span>Step Generator roll out Examples</h2>

<section id="A2.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.1 </span>Example-1</h3>

<div id="A2.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A2.SS1.p1.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="49.14" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 550 49.14" width="550"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,49.14) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#404040;" fill="#404040" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 0 L 0 49.14 L 550 49.14 L 550 0 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#F9F9F9;" fill="#F9F9F9" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0.69 0.69 L 0.69 30.28 L 549.31 30.28 L 549.31 0.69 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 12.5 34.91)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:37.94em;--ltx-fo-height:0.69em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:10pt;" height="9.61" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.61)" width="524.98"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A2.SS1.p1.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:37.94em;">
<span id="A2.SS1.p1.pic1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.p1.pic1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#FFFFFF;">ARM Rollout</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 12.5 12.03)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:37.94em;--ltx-fo-height:0.75em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.25em;font-size:10pt;" height="13.84" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 10.38)" width="524.98"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A2.SS1.p1.pic1.2" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:37.94em;">
<span id="A2.SS1.p1.pic1.2.1" class="ltx_listing ltx_lstlisting ltx_listing"><span class="ltx_listing_data"><a href="data:text/plain;base64," download="">⬇</a></span>
